 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? About one liter per hour is a good rule of thumb. More in the hot summer, less in cold winter. Take a bottle at each stop, and carry a few spare bottles for long rides. A little energy gel or a bar about every hour keeps the hunger at bay. Strong tastes in your pocket for when you feel like it. Most people can't, especially on cold legs. Your body wants a proper meal, not just caffeine.",
